      "content": "The West End currently presents as a dense, vibrant, and highly lived-in neighborhood characterized by its established tapestry of lower-income residents and historic, aging housing stock. While this density reflects a strong community presence, the district exhibits organizational challenges and disinvestment, particularly evidenced by struggling local small businesses. This existing character, while authentic, does not align with the modern infrastructural standards of the adjacent tech corridor, necessitating strategic revitalization to unlock its full potential.",
